cessful  [Music]  heat coming also from that milieu  in warsaw the  it is  worthwhile to mention also a very tragic  fate of anjiv was during  holocaust he he was  close in warsaw ghetto and  there are different variants of  his deaths one of them is saying that  his friends make the whole action  to take him out from warsaw ghetto but  when he saw german soldiers he went to  panic and was shut down  at the spot  we don't know exactly how how it was  but he he perished  in in that time in warsaw  what about  [Music]  the laters  history of our song  it is still popular in  poland you may find it in  such productions as  the tv series  a godliness borja botswana very popular  in poland in the 90s  or recent of last century  but mainly  the living of of this song and  composition  is because  it's popul its popularity is because  uh the performance by taloush can turn  the death  class from 1975.  and there is an anecdote behind it why  cantor  use this melody in his performance  it was his wife maria stangert  who was humming during  the  presence in one of the krakow's cafe  uh having this melody and cantor  immediately said  oh this is the melody for our  performance  why i think that it was  the the whole performance which is one  of the most important  performance of 20th century not only  polish theater  the reason for that i think is that the  whole performance  is about coming back to our childhood  time to our school time  to revoke the memories also traumatic  memories from that  very time and this melody serves  on that there in in that  in in this case very  strongly so when we think today  about uh vals francois it's very much  about coming back to our  childhood to our past  with the nostalgia with this kind of  feeling  we we still have  of returning to better  times uh to the golden age  something like that and precisely  that was the reason country use  for this very dramatic performance and  and there is no other music in the  performance only it's l